# Dependencies
node_modules/
.pnp
.pnp.js

# Build output. Anchored: an unanchored build/ also matches scripts/build/, the
# phase directory, and would silently drop a new script added there. The Angular
# emit sits inside the layer it belongs to, and every walker that reaches it
# excludes emittedTree() from lib/arena/layers.ts, anchored for the same reason.
/dist/
/frameworks/angular/build/
/.cache/

# The two assembled npm packages. Unlike the payload below, a package is served from
# the registry rather than from the git tag, and CI rebuilds it from the tagged
# sources, so committing it would only make every diff unreadable. Every gate that
# walks frameworks/ skips a directory named dist for the same reason.
/frameworks/react/dist/
/frameworks/angular/dist/

# Build products a script under scripts/ rewrites. The .generated. infix says a script
# writes the file; this block says which of those are untracked. Rebuild them with
# `bun run build` -- see scripts/build/README.md.
#
# A generated file is tracked for one of two reasons. The git tag has to serve it to a
# browser directly: contracts/design-generated/ and the assets/fonts/ binaries, because the
# Claude Code plugin is served from the tag and ignoring them would ship one whose
# intro/styles.css @imports resolve to nothing, unstyled and with no console error. Or a
# clone cannot reproduce it: assets/fonts/Fonts.generated.json, whose rebuild needs the
# network, the same reason UNMARKED already gives the .woff2 binaries themselves.
# Everything a script writes under frameworks/ is read by Arena's own tooling or assembled
# into a package, and is ignored. Each reason lives beside its pattern in UNTRACKED, in
# scripts/check/arena/check-generated.ts.
#
# The pattern reaches a .generated. name and nothing else, which is why the consumer branch's
# generated indexes, frameworks/SKILL.md and one per layer, need no exception here: they are
# tracked by default. They have to be, being the first thing an agent reads from the tag,
# where nothing runs a build, and check:skills asserts it because no other gate can:
# check:generated scans no .md.
/frameworks/**/*.generated.*

# Logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# Environment
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# Editor / OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*~

# Misc
.thumbnail
coverage/

# SDD scratch (ledger, task briefs, review packages) is machine-local, not product.
.superpowers/

# Specs and implementation plans, deleted once executed. What survives is the commit, the gate
# and the AGENTS.md, never the plan, which is the same intent .superpowers/ above carries.
# Tracking them would also put every plan inside the git tag that serves the Claude Code plugin.
# It sat under "Editor / OS" between .vscode/ and .thumbnail, where it read as a misfile rather
# than a decision. check:citations refuses a tracked document citing a file under here, since an
# ignored path is one no clone can follow.
docs/

# Claude Code local settings and task lock, machine-local, not product.
.claude/
